        "title": "Interesting",
        "text": "This was a very interesting location. The fee to get in was the highest I paid: 1000 nrs for a westerner and the first time I learned about the \"tour guide\" problem for western (and female) tourists in Nepal. I had someone approach me who wanted to show me around all the sights. This was common in many of the other sights I went to see and I learned how to say a firm no (which in Nepal is essentially saying \" I don't need\". )\n\nAs a non-Hindu, I could not enter the temple, but did see the rest of the complex. I went in the late afternoon, so I was the only westerner there. I would recommend going earlier if you are traveling solo.",
