        "title": "A visit with Sadhus",
        "text": "There is an area at the Pashupatinath temple where the Sadhus sleep, cook a meal and rest. It likely served as horse stables in the past, but are well suited for housing the humble Sadhu. There are two I like to chat with… one has lived at Pashupatinath for about 25 years. The other is an 86 year old Sadhu. He had a middle aged woman helping him.  There are a couple of Sadhus who don't like to have they photos taken and they will make clear their objections.\n\nGJS",
