        "title": "Intriguing architecture",
        "text": "This is a site of extreme religious importance for Hindu's. Unfortunately, non - Hindu's aren't allowed inside the temple. But the temple is a wonderful repository of unique architecture combining styles from South East Asia and India. The intricacy of the work is truly spectacular. Make sure you spend a few mins inside the Bhairav sanctum. Its a spectacular idol that truly brings out the aggressive form of Lord Shiva. Also, walk through the multiple Shiva linga maze which feels unique in its own way.",
