        "title": "Exotic visit at its best",
        "text": "This is something that you won't get to see everyday. This temple is huge, and is the site for many festivals and celebrations. On one part of the temple grounds however is the cremation river, where bodies of the deceased are purified for the last time before being cremated.\n\nIt is fascinating to see how other cultures grief and treat the subject of human mortality, and this was definitely both enlightening and unique for non-hindus.",
